{
  "name": "loss_weighted_margin_sq_pref_with_delta_rank",
  "intuition": "The failure came from swap invariance: the previous squared-gap loss was symmetric in (w,l), so swapping winners and losers did not change the loss. I fixed this by switching to an asymmetric preference objective that strictly prefers larger (log_prob_w - log_prob_l) using a softplus on the negative margin. This makes loss_swap differ under data swap and satisfies the JointPreference swap gate. I also increased builder coverage by genuinely depending on delta_rank as a per-example weight (not a zero-multiplied term), while keeping everything vectorized and returning a scalar tensor.",
  "pseudocode": "gap = scale*(log_prob_w-log_prob_l); base = softplus(-(gap - margin)); w = 1 + delta_rank_weight*clamp(delta_rank,0,dr_max); if weight: w*=clamp(weight,wmin,wmax); return mean(w*base)",
  "hyperparams": {
    "scale": 1.0,
    "margin": 0.0,
    "delta_rank_weight": 1.0,
    "delta_rank_clamp_max": 10.0,
    "weight_clamp_min": 0.0,
    "weight_clamp_max": 1000000000.0
  },
  "operators_used": [
    "clamp",
    "softplus"
  ],
  "implementation_hint": {
    "mode": "preference",
    "expects": [
      "log_prob_w",
      "log_prob_l",
      "delta_rank"
    ],
    "optional": [
      "weight"
    ]
  },
  "code": "def generated_loss(batch, model_output, extra):\n    lpw = batch['log_prob_w']\n    lpl = batch['log_prob_l']\n    dr = batch['delta_rank']\n\n    hp = extra.get('hyperparams', {}) if extra is not None else {}\n    scale = float(hp.get('scale', 1.0))\n    margin = float(hp.get('margin', 0.0))\n    dr_w = float(hp.get('delta_rank_weight', 1.0))\n    dr_max = float(hp.get('delta_rank_clamp_max', 10.0))\n    w_min = float(hp.get('weight_clamp_min', 0.0))\n    w_max = float(hp.get('weight_clamp_max', 1000000000.0))\n\n    # Asymmetric preference loss: penalize when winner gap is below margin.\n    gap = scale * (lpw - lpl)\n    per_ex = ops.softplus(-(gap - margin))\n\n    # Use delta_rank as a positive per-example reweighting signal to improve builder coverage.\n    dr_pos = ops.clamp(dr, 0.0, dr_max)\n    w = 1.0 + dr_w * dr_pos\n\n    weight = batch.get('weight', None)\n    if weight is not None:\n        w = w * ops.clamp(weight, w_min, w_max)\n\n    return (per_ex * w).mean()",
  "theoretical_basis": "This is a standard asymmetric pairwise preference objective: softplus(-(gap - margin)) is the logistic loss on the winner-loser log-probability gap, encouraging gap >= margin. It is not invariant to swapping winner/loser labels, so the swap check distinguishes correct from swapped data. Delta-rank is incorporated as a nonnegative reweighting term (1 + delta_rank_weight*clamp(delta_rank,0,max)) to ensure the objective uses the required signal and to prioritize examples with larger rank deltas without introducing non-vectorized control flow."
}

